WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.980
Agent Lane’s eyes scanned over the document
he’d been sent.

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:08.849
The decryption program had finished unraveling
the sensitive data that the SCP Foundation’s

00:00:08.849 --> 00:00:11.840
cyber security kept hidden beneath layers
of encryption.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:16.670
It had been a few hours since he’d received
the leaked document, sent to him from a mole

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:20.900
that had been active within the ranks of Foundation
personnel for some time.

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:23.710
And as for what was on this secret document?

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:30.460
It was an intake list, the records and names
of everyone recently brought into D Class.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:35.610
Lane scoured the rows upon rows of inmates,
violent criminals, the worst of the worst

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:38.360
that the Foundation used as human lab rats.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:44.210
Then, his eyes settled over one name, the
exact one he’d been looking for: the true

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:49.850
identity of a man codenamed ‘The Hatchet’,
a mass murderer, responsible for co-ordinating

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:52.829
multiple acts of international terrorism.

00:00:52.829 --> 00:00:59.160
But to Agent Lane, this man wasn’t a threat
to be feared: he was bait in a trap for something

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.079
far worse.

00:01:01.079 --> 00:01:05.820
The Global Occult Coalition had long been
the face of officially sanctioned legitimacy

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:08.060
in the fight against the anomalous.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:13.450
While the SCP Foundation operated in a more
clandestine fashion, the GOC was operated

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:17.220
by and acted under the authority of the United
Nations.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:23.329
They were mandated with policing the paranormal
world, a role nobody in the GOC took lightly.

00:01:23.329 --> 00:01:28.510
Their ultimate goal was a world rid of all
anomalies; while the Foundation opted for

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:32.250
containment, the Coalition preferred extermination.

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:37.050
But despite this fundamental difference in
their operational structures, the two organizations

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:42.650
maintained a fragile alliance… which was
why Agent Lane needed bait in order for his

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:44.530
plan to work.

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:50.700
The objective was simple: kill SCP-096, also
known as the Shy Guy.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:56.070
An anomalous entity with a long, disproportionate
human body that could use impossible speeds

00:01:56.070 --> 00:02:00.710
to kill anyone that looked at its face: even
through an image.

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:07.899
That was what worried the GOC, it seemed all
too easy for SCP-096 to be used as a weapon,

00:02:07.899 --> 00:02:10.610
especially for assassinations.

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:14.989
It wouldn’t take much for the Foundation
to mail a photo of SCP-096 to anyone, say

00:02:14.989 --> 00:02:19.520
a politician who opposed them, or the head
of another Group of Interest.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:26.040
Then, all they’d have to do is sit back
and wait as SCP-096 dispatched its unwitting

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:29.930
target, along with any witnesses that happened
to see it appear.

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:34.990
So, the Coalition had decided it was time
to take the Shy Guy off the board, before

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:38.480
anyone got any unsavory ideas.

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:41.019
But there was still one issue with that.

00:02:41.019 --> 00:02:46.410
Given the GOC and SCP Foundation’s rocky
relationship, Agent Lane had been instructed

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:49.370
to leave no trace of the Coalition’s involvement.

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:55.670
He needed someone else to be responsible for
the actual elimination of SCP-096, so that

00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:59.180
the GOC could deny any and all involvement.

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:04.540
That was when he’d gotten the idea, who
better to call on for a covert, strictly off-the-books

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:05.540
mission?

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:10.620
Only one of the world’s most elite special
forces units, with no affiliation to the GOC

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.840
whatsoever: Delta Force.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:17.819
Engineering a scenario where Lane could get
the Deltas to take out SCP-096 was going to

00:03:17.819 --> 00:03:18.830
be tricky.

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:22.760
He couldn’t give them a direct order to
kill the creature, that could too easily lead

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:24.180
back to the GOC.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:29.200
So, the mastermind behind this mission needed
to think outside the box: how could he get

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.240
the attention of Delta Force?

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:35.769
Well, by offering up one of the world’s
most wanted terrorists.

00:03:35.769 --> 00:03:40.459
After all, Delta Force was renowned for undertaking
missions that involved counter-terrorism,

00:03:40.459 --> 00:03:45.350
as well as the securing – and sometimes
elimination – of high-value targets.

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:49.099
And that was where The Hatchet came into the
plan.

00:03:49.099 --> 00:03:53.480
Given the severity and extreme nature of his
many crimes, he was certainly considered high

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:55.209
value by the US Government.

00:03:55.209 --> 00:03:59.670
However, it was while awaiting trial that
the Hatchet had disappeared under mysterious

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:00.910
circumstances.

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:05.350
The official story was he had died in prison
following a fight with another inmate, but

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:07.790
rumors circulated about an escape attempt.

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:10.670
Of course, neither were correct.

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:14.170
Now Agent Lane knew the truth: the Foundation
had him.

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:17.160
Which meant he was within the reach of the
GOC.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:22.389
Issuing a coded command to his mole working
inside the SCP Foundation, Lane instructed

00:04:22.389 --> 00:04:26.760
that the Hatchet would be making an escape
of sorts; at least, that’s how it would

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:27.760
appear.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:30.289
But it would really be completely staged.

00:04:30.289 --> 00:04:34.611
Under the cover of night, the mole drugged
and kidnapped the Hatchet, breaking open an

00:04:34.611 --> 00:04:38.520
air vent and making it look like someone had
crawled their way through.

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:43.680
Nobody had, and instead, the Hatchet was carried,
unconscious, to a Foundation vehicle the mole

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:48.160
had hotwired; if he drove off in his own car,
the Foundation would be able to trace the

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:51.949
escape back to him, and then the GOC.

00:04:51.949 --> 00:04:56.460
Bundling the terrorist into the trunk, the
mole drove several miles away from the Foundation

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:59.660
site, to an extraction point where Agent Lane
was waiting.

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:03.740
“So, he’s how you’re going to lure out
the Delta Force,” the mole said as he and

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:05.350
Lane lifted the Hatchet aboard a chopper.

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:08.729
“But how are you going to be SCP-096 to
come too?

00:05:08.729 --> 00:05:11.419
The Foundation keeps it crying in that cell.”

00:05:11.419 --> 00:05:14.509
“They can’t stop it getting out when somebody
sees it, though, right?”

00:05:14.509 --> 00:05:15.509
Lane replied.

00:05:15.509 --> 00:05:18.509
“Yeah, it moves way too fast,” the mole
confirmed.

00:05:18.509 --> 00:05:21.569
“All somebody has to do is look at it, and
it can get out, even when-”

00:05:21.569 --> 00:05:26.360
“Even when they look at a picture of it,”
the agent finished his sentence.

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:30.580
“Oh,” the mole gasped, realization spreading
across his face.

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:35.319
“Our friend the Hatchet here isn’t just
bait to lure out Delta Force,” Agent Lane

00:05:35.319 --> 00:05:36.319
explained.

00:05:36.319 --> 00:05:42.639
“He’s bait for both; SCP-096 and Delta
will both be coming after him.

00:05:42.639 --> 00:05:47.740
That way, as far as the Foundation knows,
SCP-096 will be killed during a standard Delta

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:51.020
Force mission to recapture an on-the-run terrorist
mastermind.

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:54.449
And meanwhile, the GOC gets complete deniability.

00:05:54.449 --> 00:05:58.000
It was nothing to do with us; we weren’t
involved.”

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.380
“Perfect scapegoat,” the mole commented.

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:05.340
“Thing is, if this is meant to be such a
covert mission, then why risk security by

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:06.340
telling me?”

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:11.289
“Dead men don’t talk,” Agent Lane replied
quietly, pulling a silenced handgun from his

00:06:11.289 --> 00:06:15.569
holster and squeezing the trigger, firing
three times for good measure.

00:06:15.569 --> 00:06:20.140
With the loose end tied up, nothing linked
the Global Occult Coalition to the Hatchet’s

00:06:20.140 --> 00:06:21.160
apparent ‘escape’.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:24.720
Sure enough, the Foundation fell for it hook,
line, and sinker.

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:28.940
While they were busy locking down the facility,
searing the air vents that they believed their

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:33.880
D Class prisoner had escaped through, Agent
Lane had the Hatchet handcuffed, securely

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:35.990
under lock and key.

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:40.060
The helicopter took them a short distance
to a quiet airstrip, where they boarded an

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:42.440
unchartered plane to a safehouse.

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:47.090
To avoid any further links to the GOC, Lane
had to transport the Hatchet as off the grid

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:50.750
as possible, until he got him to their destination.

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:55.360
Even that, the safehouse, couldn’t be one
the GOC had ever used before.

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:59.720
Any link and the Foundation, or Delta Force,
would smell a rat.

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:04.099
The leaked intelligence that was soon received
by Delta Force seemed to confirm their worst

00:07:04.099 --> 00:07:09.479
fears: not only was the Hatchet still alive,
but he was free and apparently hiding out

00:07:09.479 --> 00:07:10.950
in a safehouse.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:14.550
While they would never publicly acknowledge
the unit’s activities, the Department of

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:19.970
Defence issued an objective to Delta Force:
track down the Hatchet to his current location

00:07:19.970 --> 00:07:22.470
and either capture him, or kill him.

00:07:22.470 --> 00:07:26.830
A squad of some of the most highly trained
United States troops were assembled.

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:31.259
Before joining Delta Force, most of them had
been recruited from the elite 75th Ranger

00:07:31.259 --> 00:07:35.780
Regiment, as well as from other branches of
Special Forces and the wider US Army.

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:39.520
The team wasn’t told by their commander
– whose identity was classified – where

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:40.650
they were going.

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:44.870
All the information they were given was only
the essentials; just that there was a high-value

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:46.990
target holed up in a safehouse.

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:51.690
Although they had no idea there would actually
be two; only the second was unlike anything

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:54.190
the Deltas had ever seen…

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:58.300
Agent Lane was watching over hidden infrared
cameras; they were set to cut out the minute

00:07:58.300 --> 00:07:59.860
the lights came on.

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:05.509
No point in going to all this trouble only
to see SCP-096 on his feed and be killed too.

00:08:05.509 --> 00:08:09.500
Silently, using all the skills in stealth
that they’d been trained in, the squad of

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:12.199
Delta Force operators slipped into the safehouse.

00:08:12.199 --> 00:08:17.590
Their movements were perfectly synchronized,
practiced hours and hours at a time.

00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:21.810
They checked corners, two would sweep one
room of the building whilst two more protected

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:26.840
them, and none of them would move on until
they’d confirmed the area was clear.

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:31.130
Floor by floor, they worked their way up the
building, ascending closer and closer to where

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:32.460
the Hatchet was.

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:36.519
The operators were fully expecting to meet
armed resistance from the Hatchet’s loyalists

00:08:36.519 --> 00:08:40.770
when they arrived; the fact the place was
so quiet didn’t seem right.

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:45.140
In fact, none of the lights were on either,
the Delta Force unit needed to wear night

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:47.820
vision just to navigate their way around.

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:52.089
Despite it seeming suspicious, none of them
could have guessed it was intentional: Agent

00:08:52.089 --> 00:08:55.279
Lane had set everything up to work perfectly.

00:08:55.279 --> 00:08:59.810
Arriving at one room, the special forces troops
could hear the sound of someone behind the

00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:00.810
door.

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:03.820
Their voice was muffled, like something was
obstructing their mouth and preventing them

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:05.170
from speaking.

00:09:05.170 --> 00:09:09.730
This was it, the team lined up against the
nearest wall and placed an explosive charge

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:10.730
on the door.

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:15.890
With a mighty explosion, the entrance burst
wide open and the team filed in, weapons trained

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:18.100
on the room’s sole occupant.

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:23.140
They could see, through the hazy green of
their goggles, a figure sat in a chair…

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:27.370
no, restrained to a chair, with something
in front of him.

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:30.649
It looked like a frame, a photograph in a
frame.

00:09:30.649 --> 00:09:32.990
Who sits in front of a photo in the dark?

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:36.800
Suddenly, the lights came up, causing the
operators’ night vision goggles to beam

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:39.270
bright white straight into their eyes.

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:43.300
The second the lights came on, the cameras
Agent Lane was watching through cut off, and

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:48.260
he purged the hard drive they were connected
to, leaving no recording, no evidence of the

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:50.459
situation he’d engineered.

00:09:50.459 --> 00:09:54.700
Meanwhile, as the room was illuminated, the
first of the Delta Force team to take off

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:57.649
his goggles saw who it was tied to the chair.

00:09:57.649 --> 00:10:03.221
It was the Hatchet, bound by his wrists and
ankles, eyes pried open so he couldn’t look

00:10:03.221 --> 00:10:08.680
away from the framed photo in front of him…
a photo of SCP-096.

00:10:08.680 --> 00:10:13.620
Suddenly, within the blink of an eye, the
tall, slender creature had appeared in the

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:15.579
room with the captive terrorist.

00:10:15.579 --> 00:10:20.620
The Deltas, removing their goggles, turned
in horror to see SCP-096 slaughter their target.

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:26.100
And the moment they looked at it, the wailing
Shy Guy started bearing down on them too.

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:27.350
“Contact!”

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:28.430
their captain yelled.

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:30.829
“Open fire, hostile contact!”

00:10:30.829 --> 00:10:35.010
They started shooting, their bullets having
little effect on the looming, wiry monster

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:37.980
as it came at each of the squad, one by one.

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:42.151
The muzzle flashes illuminated the oncoming
anomaly, those brief glimpses of it in the

00:10:42.151 --> 00:10:45.790
flickering of gunfire made it look all the
more horrifying.

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:51.390
Screams filled the room, echoing through the
building as SCP-096 decimated the team that

00:10:51.390 --> 00:10:54.110
had unknowingly been sent in to kill it.

00:10:54.110 --> 00:10:58.470
One of the Deltas was still struggling with
his night vision, unable to detach them from

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:01.220
his face thanks to a clasp that had gotten
stuck.

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:05.339
All he could hear were his squad mates around
him being killed, but with no way of seeing

00:11:05.339 --> 00:11:07.060
what was happening.

00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:08.290
“Private!”

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:12.791
the captain gurgled; he sounded hurt, but
the operator couldn’t see how badly, or

00:11:12.791 --> 00:11:14.250
what had attacked him.

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:15.360
“Shoot this thing!

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:16.480
Shoot it now!”

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:21.550
“I can’t see, sir!” he yelled back,
goggles still strapped to his face, eyes shut

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:23.380
to keep out the searing whiteness.

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:24.720
“Ten o’clock!”

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:28.970
the captain replied, directing his subordinate
to aim his weapon slightly to the left.

00:11:28.970 --> 00:11:32.940
There was a sickening twisting sound, and
the Captain’s voice cut out.

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:35.790
The Private fired, his shot winging the creature.

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:40.230
It whimpered, then seemed to vanish as quickly
as it had arrived.

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:44.800
Pulling a combat knife from a sheath on his
belt, the operator was able to cut the strap

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:46.820
keeping the goggles over his eyes.

00:11:46.820 --> 00:11:52.260
When his vision cleared, he looked around
to see an empty room, smeared in blood.

00:11:52.260 --> 00:11:56.610
Even the Hatchet hadn’t survived, killed
in the chair he’d been held in.

00:11:56.610 --> 00:12:00.530
The operator took a closer look at the photo
the terrorist had been made to look directly

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:01.530
at.

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:03.920
It was hideous, tall, and thin.

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:06.420
arms that looked too long and a huge mouth.

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:08.670
And now it was behind him.

00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:09.670
He’d gotten lucky, it had left the Private
alone because he hadn’t seen it.

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:10.670
But now he had, and SCP-096 knew.

00:12:10.670 --> 00:12:11.670
It always knew, and despite the best efforts
of those trying to stop it, it would never

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:13.149
stop killing anyone that looked at it.

